<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oreshek Fortress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1323">1323</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Oreshek, Shlisselburg Fortress, Nöteborg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oreshek is a fortress on an island at the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva River</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, founded by Novgorod in 1323. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-noteborg">Treaty of Nöteborg</a>, the first border agreement between Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, was signed there the same year. Held by Sweden as Nöteborg from 1612, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1702 and renamed Shlisselburg, later serving as a notorious political prison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oreshek-fortress.jpg" alt="Oreshek Fortress" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moneycantbuy · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BF%D0%BE%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C_%D0%9E%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%88%D0%B5%D0%BA._%D0%93._%D0%A8%D0%BB%D0%B8%D1%81%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B1%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B3_(%D0%A1%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%BA%D1%82-%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%82%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B1%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B3)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
